{"parentUuid":"1ba78351-8c0d-4f83-a9d9-7344bf66bdc0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"ae75cc2fe613b3186","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ws6ypBHiErhZ4AnNtfcnT5","type":"tool_result","content":"f860ff3 codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\nbd7e1e2 rules: a recording outranks a doc; partial support is supported with deviations; unsupported may be shown by runs (#90)\ncfd2711 rules: judge per unit (subjects), module.yaml is the agent's, module-distinct (#89)\nstatement: >-\n  What hooks do leaves records in the session transcript: a silent success\n  leaves nothing, while errors, blocks, cancellations and the context a hook\n  adds are recorded, and each stop that ran hooks ends with a summary record.\n  (Where context too long to keep goes is hook-additional-context's, and\n  a stop hook that gives context without blocking is not part of this.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-0\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#other-exit-codes\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#add-context-for-claude\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookmix\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgbash\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout\n  codex: pending\n  cursor: pending\ncommit f860ff366b50328d62a3ff06a1cd76d39e84245f\nAuthor: Mykyta Svyrydenko <<redacted-email>>\nDate:   Sat Oct 3 16:44:15 2026 +0200\n\n    codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\n    \n    Codex tells the agent a failed command's output like a success's; the failure is only in the event stream's command_execution item (status failed, exit_code). Recorded with the real codex; the cell lists that as a deviation, and the mock does the same.\n    \n    Co-authored-by: