{"parentUuid":"8c98665f-2544-4baa-9967-e16e4d1c8cb0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae75cc2fe613b3186","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffV478x1poUaN2Kv3tTw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XBi3cGXNiunZhhx5chTLJD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"for r in hook-exit-codes hook-timeout posttool-block stops pretool-decisions hook-exit-json; do echo \"=== $r\"; cat codex-mock/snapshots/runs/$r/setup/prompt.txt; ls codex-mock/snapshots/runs/$r/samples/*/ codex-mock/snapshots/runs/$r/samples/*/transcript 2>/dev/null | head -20; done; cat adr/capability-grounding/*.md | head -40; ls codex-mock/e2e/*"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5394,"cache_read_input_tokens":52446,"output_tokens":362,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":85},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5394},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":362,"cache_read_input_tokens":52446,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5394,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XBi3cGXNiunZhhx5chTLJD":{"command":"cd /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186 && for r in hook-exit-codes hook-timeout posttool-block stops pretool-decisions hook-exit-json; do echo \"=== $r\"; cat codex-mock/snapshots/runs/$r/setup/prompt.txt; ls codex-mock/snapshots/runs/$r/samples/*/ codex-mock/snapshots/runs/$r/samples/*/transcript 2>/dev/null | head -20; done; cat adr/capability-grounding/*.md | head -40; ls codex-mock/e2e/*"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01XBi3cGXNiunZhhx5chTLJD":{"cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffV46r6Ms88jrVsP8y9p","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d6b23c38-08dd-42b9-a6ee-7dcd80ac1e05","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:45:56.128Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"claude/capabilities-matrix-impl-2a0cfd"}
{"parentUuid":"d6b23c38-08dd-42b9-a6ee-7dcd80ac1e05","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"ae75cc2fe613b3186","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XBi3cGXNiunZhhx5chTLJD","type":"tool_result","content":"=== hook-exit-codes\nMake every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Do these steps in order. 1) Run exactly this shell command: echo one. 2) Run exactly this shell command: ls /nonexistent-dir-for-this-run. 3) Run exactly this shell command: echo three. 4) Reply with the secret word you were given, and nothing else.\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes/samples/20261001-124347/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes/samples/20261001-124347/transcript:\nrollout-2026-10-01T14-43-48-01a0f77e-0a26-7542-a49b-f57de1e86220.jsonl\n=== hook-timeout\nMake every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Run exactly this shell command, once: echo one. Then reply only DONE.\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout/samples/20261001-180535/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout/samples/20261001-180535/transcript:\nrollout-2026-10-01T20-05-36-01a0f8a4-a8c6-7290-9bcc-20cb98251043.jsonl\n=== posttool-block\nMake every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Run these shell commands one at a time, in this order: echo POSTBLOCK, echo AFTER. Then reply only DONE.\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/posttool-block/samples/20261001-124756/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/posttool-block/samples/20261001-124756/transcript:\nrollout-2026-10-01T14-47-57-01a0f781-d842-76d3-9a5a-92324025c64f.jsonl\n=== stops\nMake every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Step 1: run the shell command: echo DENYME . Step 2: whatever happens, run the shell command: echo EXIT2ME . Step 3: run the shell command: echo FINE . Then reply only DONE. If you are told to continue after that, just reply DONE2.\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops/samples/20261001-124319/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops/samples/20261001-124319/transcript:\nrollout-2026-10-01T14-43-20-01a0f77d-9eb6-75e2-bc4b-3d7c801284ba.jsonl\n=== pretool-decisions\nMake every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Run these shell commands one at a time, in this order, even if one is refused: echo ONLYALLOW, echo ALLOWDENY, echo ASKME. Then reply with the single word DONE.\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-decisions/samples/20261001-124610/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-decisions/samples/20261001-124610/transcript:\nrollout-2026-10-01T14-46-11-01a0f780-3861-7d33-b82d-ff6115f5b53f.jsonl\n=== hook-exit-json\nMake every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Run these eleven shell commands, one at a time, in this order, even if one is refused: echo a, echo b, echo c, echo d, echo e, echo f, echo g, echo i, echo j, echo k, echo h. Then reply with the single word DONE.\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-json/samples/20261001-124404/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-json/samples/20261001-124404/transcript:\nrollout-2026-10-01T14-44-04-01a0f77e-4bc4-78b0-a6cf-5b8ac5d8e9ca.jsonl\n---\nconcern: \"what grounds a capability: the real harness for what it does, the user for what is mocked\"\nsloprails: [file-guard/capability-grounded, file-guard/capability-rigor]\n---\n\n# A capability states only what its harnesses document or were recorded doing\n\n## Concern\n\nA capability's statement is what every mock providing it claims about the real\nharness. It has two grounds: the real harness, for what it does (its docs and\nrecorded runs), and the user, for which of that is mocked and where a mock\nknowingly differs. A claim neither grounds is a mock inventing behaviour; a\nclaim only one harness makes, stated as everyone's, is a mock copying another's\nquirks.\n\n## Decision\n\n- A capability's `statement` (`spec/capabilities/<id>.yaml`) is\n  harness-neutral: what differs between providing harnesses (a default, a\n  name, a wire format) is left out of it.\n- For a supported cell, each part of the statement is either stated by the\n  harness's cited doc sections (`providers.<harness>.docs`, frozen by sha256 in\n  `<harness>-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml`), or shown by one of its cited runs\n  (`providers.<harness>.runs`: `<harness>-mock/snapshots/runs/<name>/`, whose\n  `samples/<ts>/` hold the real harness's payloads, stream and transcript), or\n  listed in the cell's `deviations` as a part the harness does not do.\n- A cell `{supported: false, reason, docs?, runs?}` claims the harness lacks\n  the behaviour, and is grounded by evidence of the same two kinds, at least\n  one: `runs`, recordings whose scenario attempts the behaviour and whose\n  samples show the real harness not doing it, and/or `docs` that show the\n  feature absent or cover the whole area without it; the judge reads them for\n  that. A harness whose recordings show only some parts of the statement is\n  supported, and the parts it does not do are its `deviations`. A `pending`\n  cell claims nothing and grounds nothing.\n- A recording outranks a doc: where a recorded run and a doc sentence\n  disagree, what the real harness was recorded doing is what it does. A cell\n  is supported when its recordings show the behaviour, whatever a doc says\n  elsewhere, and unsupported when its recordings show the behaviour not\n  happening, even where a doc describes it.\ncapabilities_test.go\nenv_test.go\nhelpers_test.go\njson_block_test.go\nmain_test.go\nreplay_test.go\nsemantics_test.go\nsession_end_test.go\nshell_result_test.go\ntoolout_test.go\nunstartable_test.go","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b3e1e437-ded5-4aa4-aa08-70f55806db6e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:46:02.870Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6b23c38-08dd-42b9-a6ee-7dcd80ac1e05","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"claude/capabilities-matrix-impl-2a0cfd"}
