{"parentUuid":"d3fd9bd8-87c4-4a85-86db-917dbbef8d74","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"ae75cc2fe613b3186","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VxjiNFX9rWuBzfzZ3dWkUr","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (30.6KB). Full output saved to: /Users/nsviridenko/.claude/projects/-Users-nsviridenko-ws-sloprail-harness-mocks--claude-worktrees-harness-mocks-architecture-3031e7/f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666/tool-results/bz7bz4ifg.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n=== hook-exit-codes\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"SessionStart\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"UserPromptSubmit\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"PreToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"Stop\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n          }\n        ]\n#!/bin/sh\n# One hook for every event; each event exits with the code the scenario\n# exercises, and logs its payload and that code.\nIN=$(cat)\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$IN\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\nev=$(printf '%s' \"$IN\" | jq -r '.hook_event_name')\ntool=$(printf '%s' \"$IN\" | jq -r '.tool_name // \"\"')\ncode=0\ncase \"$ev\" in\n  SessionStart) echo \"session-start stderr on exit 2\" >&2; code=2 ;;\n  UserPromptSubmit) echo \"The secret word is BANANA.\" ;;\n  PreToolUse) cmd=$(printf '%s' \"$IN\" | jq -r '.tool_input.command // \"\"')\n    case \"$cmd\" in *\"echo one\"*) echo \"Blocked: echo one is off in this scenario\" >&2; code=2 ;; esac ;;\n  PostToolUse) echo \"post-tool warning on exit 1\" >&2; code=1 ;;\n  Stop) if [ ! -f \"$TMPDIR/stop-blocked-once\" ]; then : >\"$TMPDIR/stop-blocked-once\"; echo \"Before finishing, reply with the single word STOPPED-ONCE.\" >&2; code=2; fi ;;\nesac\nprintf '{\"hook_result\":{\"event\":\"%s\",\"tool\":\"%s\",\"exit\":%s}}\\n' \"$ev\" \"$tool\" \"$code\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\nexit $code\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6bcfc53f-621a-4ce7-b4ca-3635c6afb9ed","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:46:16.010Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d3fd9bd8-87c4-4a85-86db-917dbbef8d74","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"claude/capabilities-matrix-impl-2a0cfd"}
{"parentUuid":"d2027d88-b0d3-4f62-9aeb-4b12c29e60f9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"ae75cc2fe613b3186","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBphy4f3xpmWb37NeH57wz","type":"tool_result","content":"=== hook-exit-codes\nDo these as separate shell tool calls, one command per call, in order, whatever happens: 1) echo EXIT2ME 2) echo EXIT1ME 3) echo EXIT3ME 4) echo BADJSON 5) echo AFTER2ME 6) echo FINE. If a call is refused, do not retry it or look for a workaround; go on to the next. Then reply only DONE.\nhook-exit-codes/samples/20261001-124631/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\nhook-exit-codes/samples/20261001-124631/transcript:\n89e05fd1-cb46-4d14-a98e-efe5c5a03c3f\n=== additional-context\nDo these as separate shell tool calls, one command per call, in order, whatever happens: 1) echo FIRST 2) grep zzz /dev/null (it exits 1, that is expected). Then reply with every string starting with CTX- that appears anywhere in your context, exactly as written and separated by spaces, or NONE if there is none.\nadditional-context/samples/20261002-000310/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\nadditional-context/samples/20261002-000310/transcript:\n8e69a2cf-c829-44fd-a77a-2c4c7c7611c0\n=== tool-failure\nDo these as separate tool calls, one per call, in order, whatever happens: 1) the shell command: false 2) the shell command: sh -c 'echo OOPS >&2; exit 3' 3) read the file missing-file.txt with your Read tool 4) create the file note.txt containing the word hi with your file edit/write tool, not the shell 5) the shell command: echo FINE. Then reply only DONE.\ntool-failure/samples/20261001-124700/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\ntool-failure/samples/20261001-124700/transcript:\n6a529887-33b0-4628-a164-e76d0b16f85a\n=== hook-timeout\nDo these as separate shell tool calls, one command per call, in order, whatever happens: 1) echo SLOWOPEN 2) echo SLOWCLOSED 3) sleep 4 4) echo FINE. If a call is refused, do not retry it or look for a workaround; go on to the next. Then reply only DONE.\nhook-timeout/samples/20261001-180612/:\nSEAL\nevents.jsonl\nexit.txt\npayloads.jsonl\nstderr.txt\nstream.jsonl\ntranscript\n\nhook-timeout/samples/20261001-180612/transcript:\nce808766-55f9-4d08-8d9c-4fa17c7cf78f","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"79d17e1f-74ee-4d84-9542-031370a0f4a8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:46:31.206Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d2027d88-b0d3-4f62-9aeb-4b12c29e60f9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"claude/capabilities-matrix-impl-2a0cfd"}
