file-guard \"module-coverage\": cheap checks 22.7s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"module-leaks\": cheap checks 86ms, judges 1.23s\nsloprail: file-guard \"shapes\": cheap checks 2.198s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\": cheap checks 18.625s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\": cheap checks 7.269s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\": cheap checks 7.293s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guards evaluated in 1m47.666s (26 rules, concurrency 6)\nthe following rules refused this work:\n  - The test matches both recordings (hook-exit-codes and hook-timeout) and the deviation, but the cited Codex docs state recorded behaviours that no test or run covers. A PostToolUse block (decision:block or exit 2) 'records the feedback, replaces the tool result with that feedback'. PostToolUse hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext is added as developer context. A UserPromptSubmit block (decision:block or exit 2) blocks the prompt. A UserPromptSubmit JSON additionalContext is added as developer context. The only PostToolUse run in hook-exit-codes uses exit 1, and its UserPromptSubmit run uses plain-text stdout. Add runs and tests for these variants.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/hook_records_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, spec/capabilities/hook-output-transcript-records.yaml (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The only test, TestPostToolUsePayloadCarriesInputAndResponse (capabilities_test.go:285), covers one successful `echo FINE` Bash call. It checks tool_name, tool_input and tool_response, and nothing else. (1) The doc says PostToolUse 'also runs after commands that exit with a non-zero status', and no test covers it. (2) The runs show no PostToolUse for the PreToolUse-refused calls `echo DENYME` and `echo EXIT2ME`, and no test asserts that. (3) The runs show repeated PostToolUse firings, one per call, in posttool-block, and the test asserts only a single call. (4) The doc lists `tool_use_id` and `turn_id`, and the statement says the hook receives 'how long the call took'. The test checks none of these, and the runs record no duration.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/hook_records_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, spec/capabilities/hook-output-transcript-records.yaml (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The Codex doc (hooks#stop) says a matching Stop hook returning `continue: false` takes precedence over other Stop hooks' block decisions, and no test in capabilities_test.go exercises it (TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd only replays runs/stops with JSON and exit-2 blocks); the test also only checks that the reason appears somewhere in the rollout, not that it is handed back as a new user-prompt message, and runs/hook-exit-codes is never asserted for this capability.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/hook_records_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, spec/capabilities/hook-output-transcript-records.yaml (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing drives only two Stop events, so it never checks the recorded third Stop (stops events.jsonl, 3rd Stop line has stop_hook_active:true) staying true after two consecutive blocks, whether the first block used JSON or exit 2, or last_assistant_message on the continuation Stops; and the doc's turn_id field on Stop (and the string|null nullability of last_assistant_message) is asserted by no test.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/hook_records_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, spec/capabilities/hook-output-transcript-records.yaml (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - Checklist: (1) plain-text stdout adds context, from the doc and the hook-exit-codes run: covered by TestUserPromptSubmitAddsContextOrRefuses. (2) The payload `prompt` arrives unchanged, from the run: covered by the same test. (3) Exit 2 refuses the prompt, from the prompt-blocked run: the same test only asserts the stream shape [thread.started, turn.started, turn.completed] after replaying the recording. It never checks that the prompt did not reach the agent or that SHOULDNOTRUN was not run, and it does not check that the hook's stderr reason was captured. (4) The doc's JSON `{\"decision\":\"block\",\"reason\":...}` refusal: no test. (5) The doc's JSON `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` form: no test. (6) The doc's `turn_id` field in the UserPromptSubmit payload: no test asserts it. (7) The statement's background-task notification firing: no test. The doc-stated JSON block and additionalContext variants and the `turn_id` field are required even without a recorded run, so the subject fails.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/hook_records_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, spec/capabilities/hook-output-transcript-records.yaml (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f1483892-cd36-4f6c-bb7f-f672acd25646","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:54:23.276Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f10406f5-37bb-4e77-b437-a6f374304d36","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
