{"parentUuid":"5666a2de-b0ff-41fe-8feb-1400f00c3bed","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae75cc2fe613b3186","attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186/codex-mock/internal/session/file.go","snippet":"12\t\n13\t// File is a session's append-only rollout: one JSON record per line.\n14\ttype File struct {\n15\t\tPath string\n16\t\tf    *os.File\n17\t}\n18\t\n19\t// Create starts the rollout of session id at\n20\t// <home>/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-<time>-<id>.jsonl, with its meta record:\n21\t// keyed by the day and the session id, not by the working directory, and\n22\t// already there when the start hook runs (recorded: runs/session-transcript-file).\n23\t//\n24\t// sr:provides session-transcript-file/codex\n25\tfunc Create(home, id, cwd string, now time.Time) (*File, error) {\n26\t\tdir := filepath.Join(home, \"sessions\", now.Format(\"2006\"), now.Format(\"01\"), now.Format(\"02\"))\n27\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(dir, 0o755); err != nil {\n28\t\t\treturn nil, err\n29\t\t}\n30\t\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, fmt.Sprintf(\"rollout-%s-%s.jsonl\", now.Format(\"2006-01-02T15-04-05\"), id))\n31\t\tf, err := os.Create(path)\n32\t\tif err != nil {"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f8ee238f-b995-464c-96d1-2b601c594db9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:15:25.584Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ae75cc2fe613b3186/codex-mock/internal/session/file.go changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n12\t\n13\t// File is a session's append-only rollout: one JSON record per line.\n14\ttype File struct {\n15\t\tPath string\n16\t\tf    *os.File\n17\t}\n18\t\n19\t// Create starts the rollout